WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.900
The rack and facility must agree on what each provides.

2
00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:07.000
For power, that includes the supported operating envelope and behavior at the

3
00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:07.480
handoff.

4
00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:11.260
For cooling, it includes the conditions the receiving system can guarantee.

5
00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:15.760
Neither side should assume the other absorbs every transient or capacity shortfall.

6
00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:19.700
Identify the measurements used to assess those commitments and the owner of

7
00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:20.420
each response.

8
00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:24.860
A facility alarm, rack controller and local protection function may observe or

9
00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:26.260
act on different conditions.

10
00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:30.640
Clear responsibility prevents a gap where every team expects another system to

11
00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:31.660
make the same decision.

12
00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:35.600
Validate the combined behavior under the agreed demand and fault cases.

13
00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:39.180
Keep operating restrictions and change control in the handover record.

14
00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:44.900
The linked low-voltage distribution and grid-performance courses provide specialist depth; here the

15
00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:47.660
purpose is to make the rack-to-facility boundary explicit.

16
00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:51.560
The deployment review is complete only when the proposed rack behavior and

17
00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:53.660
the site's actual commitments fit together.

